.TH BOOP-HELPER 8 "" "Boop" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
boop-helper \- holds the Boop VPN tunnel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/boop/boop-helper
[\fB\-\-cleanup\fR] [\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boop-helper
runs as root under systemd (\fBboop-helper.service\fR). It brings up the
AmneziaWG interface \fBboop0\fR, routes all traffic into it through its own
routing table and rules (as wg-quick does), hands the DNS servers to
systemd-resolved, and takes all of it away again when the app disconnects,
quits or crashes, and when the service stops.
.PP
It listens on \fI/run/boop/helper.sock\fR and answers only root and the
members of the group \fBboop\fR (checked by the caller's uid). It can only
bring the tunnel up with a checked config, take it down, report its state and
ping an IPv4 address.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup
remove whatever a tunnel left (rules, routes, DNS settings, the interface) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
the socket to listen on.
.TP
.BI \-\-group " name"
the group whose members may use the helper.
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boop (1),
.BR resolvectl (1),
.BR ip-rule (8)
